    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0791" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-13T13:00:00+01:00">February 13, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—10:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Gilbert’s 29, February 12, 1931.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d699-f1"/>
                        Sugimura<anchor n="32" xml:id="d699-f2"/> has addressed through me to Reber
                    a formal notification of the convocation of the meeting of the Liberian
                    Committee at London, February 26th. He adds informally that he will arrange for
                    some of his colleagues to be in London by February 23 in order to have
                    preliminary talks with Reber. Reber’s notification forwarded London and Geneva
                    informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d699-f1" n="31" xml:id="d699-f1-content">
                <p>Not; printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d699-f2" n="32" xml:id="d699-f2-content">
                <p>Y. Sugimura (Japanese), Under Secretary General and Director of Political Section
                    of the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
